    puts stderr {Name   : dbus}
    puts stderr {Version: 1.13.6}
    puts stderr {Target : x86_64_v3}
    puts stderr {}
    puts stderr {D-Bus is a message bus system, a simple way for applications to talk to}
    puts stderr {one another. D-Bus supplies both a system daemon (for events such new}
    puts stderr {hardware device printer queue ) and a per-user-login-session daemon (for}
    puts stderr {general IPC needs among user applications). Also, the message bus is}
    puts stderr {built on top of a general one-to-one message passing framework, which}
    puts stderr {can be used by any two applications to communicate directly (without}
    puts stderr {going through the message bus daemon).}
}

